hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9406","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Gabriel asked permission to do so. Peace be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Come in.” He said: “How can I enter, when there is a curtain in your house in which are statues of horses and men? Either you will be cut down.” their heads, or made a rug to be stepped on, for indeed, we, the angels, do not enter a house in which there are images.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9407","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, among the people who will be most tormented on the Day of Resurrection are those who make pictures.” Ahmed said: The photographers"
"9408","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad bin Kathir al-Harrani told us, saying: Muhammad bin al-Sabbah told us, he said: Ismail bin Zakaria told us, he said: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Subayh, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among the people who will be most severely tormented on the Day of Resurrection are the photographers.” Ahmed said: The photographers (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9409","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If the length of one of you’s sandals is torn, he should not walk in just one sandal until he repairs it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9410","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Razin, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah He hits his forehead with his hand and says: O people of Iraq, you claim that I am lying to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I bear witness. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If a dog licks the bowl of one of you, let him wash it seven times, and if a one of you, let him not move on to the other until he improves it.”"
"9411","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Ibn Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If the shoe of one of you is cut off, he should not walk in a single shoe until his shoe is repaired, nor should he walk in a single shoe. He eats with his left hand, does not wear a single garment, and does not cover a single garment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9412","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawawi told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Do not wear a blind woman in one garment, nor should any of you eat with his left hand, nor should one wear a cloak in one garment.” One, and he should not walk in single shoes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9413","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Maqil told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said in a battle that we undertook: “Put on a lot of shoes, for a man will continue to ride what he has on.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9414","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us, he said: Anas told us, “Indeed, Na’al is the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had two faces.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9415","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, he said: “It was “Let us make the shoes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Qabalan,” and the shoes of Abu Bakr Qabalan, and the shoes of Omar Qabalan. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9416","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of, He heard Amr bin Harith say: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “praying in two slippers.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the following is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9417","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Suddi told us, on the authority of, Amr bin Harith heard, he said: I saw the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace. “He prays in two slippers” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9418","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Rahman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, he said: He told me who, heard Amr bin Harith, said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prays in two slippers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9419","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Omar bin Abi al-Wazir Abu Mutrif told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down on a bed, and then he sweated, so Umm Sulaim got up to wipe him off. So she dried it and put it in a bottle, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw it and said: “What is this that you are doing, O Umm Sulaym?” She said: I will put your sweat in my perfume, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9420","Al-Hasan bin Qaza’ah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, and Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not pray in our hut.” Sufyan said: Our tapestry (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9421","Al-Hasan bin Qazaa informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not pray in our halls.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9422","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Muawiyah entered When he was sick, he visited Abu Hashim bin Utbah, and he said: My uncle, what makes you cry? Is it pain that disgusts you, or is it eagerness for the world? He said: No, no, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with me, which I did not keep. He said: “Only a servant is sufficient for you in collecting money. And mounted in the path of God.” I find that today I have gathered"
"9423","Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Samurah ibn Sahm, a man from his people, who said: It was revealed: On Abu Hashim bin Utbah, he was suffering from a sick condition, so Muawiyah came to him to treat him, so Abu Hashim cried, and Muawiyah said to him: What makes you cry, my uncle? Is there a pain that disgusts you, or is it the world whose purity has gone? He said: No, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with me that I wish I had followed. He said: “Indeed, perhaps you will realize Wealth is not to be divided among peoples, and only a servant and a rider in the path of God is sufficient for you of that.” Then I realized, so I gathered (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9424","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Mawla, on the authority of Buraydah Al-Aslami, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A servant and a vehicle are sufficient for one of you in this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9425","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Amr bin Asim told us, he said: Hammam and Jarir told us, they said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “It was The sole of the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of silver, and the hat of his sword was made of silver, and everything between that was a silver earring.”"
"9426","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid told us, who is Ibn Zurai’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Al-Hasan, He said: “The cap of the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of silver.”"
"9427","Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Uthman bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, He said: “The cape of the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of silver.”"
"9428","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Shaykh, that he heard Muawiyah, and he had A group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were in the Kaaba. He said: Do you know that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade riding on “The skin of tigers?” They said: “Oh God, yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9429","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Mugheerah, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Abu Shaykh, he said: While we were with Muawiyah, when he gathered A group of the Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were in the Kaaba. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us to spread out The skins of wild animals? They said: Oh God, yes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9430","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Sheikh told me Al-Hinai, on the authority of Abu Hamman, that Muawiyah, in the year of Hajj, gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Kaaba, and he said to them: “I appealed to you by God. Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid lining up with tigers?” They said: Yes. He said: “And I bear witness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9431","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told me, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir told me, he said: he told me Abu Sheikh, on the authority of his brother Hamman, that in the year Muawiyah performed Hajj, he gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Kaaba, and he said: “ I adjure you by God, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid the formation of tigers? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9432","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Tell me. Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Sheikh told me, he said: Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba. He said: “I adjure you by God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding the ranks of tigers?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And me.” I bear witness"
"9433","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told me, he said: Amara bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, he said: He told me Hamman, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba and said: “I adjure you by God, have you not heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Did he forbid the ranks of tigers?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I bear witness.”"
"9434","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me He said: Abu Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba, and said: “I adjure you by God: Did you not hear the Messenger of Does God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbid ranks of tigers?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I bear witness.”"
"9435","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Humran told me, he said: Mu’awiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar in The Kaaba, and he said: “I adjure you by God, have you not heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the ranks of tigers?” They said: Oh God. Yes, he said: “And I bear witness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9436","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Muawiyah addressed the people, He said: I am telling you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So whatever you hear from him, believe me. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not wear gold except in pieces.” They said: We heard him. He said: And I heard him say: “Whoever rides a tiger, you will not accompany him.” “The angels.” They said: “We heard.” He said: “And I heard him forbidding pleasure.” They said: “We did not listen.” He said: “Yes, otherwise you should keep silent.”"
"9437","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Ali, he said: He told me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Say, ‘O God, guide me and guide me’,” and he forbade me from putting my ring on this little finger or the next. Asim did not know which of the two, and he forbade me from wearing robes, and from sitting on mats. As for the qisi, it is ribbed clothing brought from Egypt and the Levant, and the miter: something that women used to make for their husbands while traveling. Like marigolds of purple (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9438","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sulaiman bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Rifa’ah said: “ I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was delivering the sermon, and I said: O Messenger of God, a strange man came to ask you about his religion. He does not know. What is his religion? So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and left his sermon until he finished, and a chair was brought, the legs of which were bare. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat over him, and he began to teach me what God had taught him, then he came to his sermon and completed it.”"
"9439","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of Abu Juhayfa, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Batha, and he was in a red dome, and there were people with him walking, when Bilal came to him and gave the call to prayer.” Then he began to follow his mouth here and there.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9440","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Malik bin Amr told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in a red hood, with about forty men, and he said: “Indeed, the matter will be opened to you and you will be helped. So whoever realizes that, let him fear God, and enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong, and pray \have mercy\"""""""
"9441","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Salama bin Kuhayl told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, said: When morning came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have become on the nature of Islam. And the word of sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the religion of our father Abraham, upright and Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists.” He was succeeded by Muhammad bin Bashar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9442","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “We have adhered to common sense and sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And peace be upon him, and the religion of our father Abraham, upright and Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9443","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the morning: “We have become upon the nature of Islam, and the word Sincerity, and in the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the religion of our father Abraham, upright and Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9444","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Uqail, on the authority of Sabiq bin Najiya, on the authority of Abu Salam, he was in the Mosque of Homs, and a man passed by, so I went up to him and said: Tell me a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The men did not discuss it between you and him. He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “No Muslim servant says when he is three in the morning, And when evening comes: I am satisfied with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, as Prophet. \resurrection\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9445","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, he said: Abu Hani told me On the authority of Abu Ali al-Janabi, that he heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: I am satisfied with God usury, and Islam as religion, and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him as a messenger, and Paradise is destined for him.” He said: “So I was happy and pleased with that.” Abdullah bin Wahb disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Hani, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Saeed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9446","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading from him, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Abu Hani told me, on the authority of my father Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Sa`id, whoever is satisfied with God usury, and Islam as religion, and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as a prophet, and Paradise is guaranteed for him.” Abu Sa`id was amazed at her. He said: Give it back to me, O Messenger of God. So he did. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9447","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Anbasa, on the authority of Ibn Ghanam, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever says in the morning: Oh God, what has become of me... By a blessing or by one of Your creation, it is from You alone, with no partner to You. To You is praise and to You is gratitude, unless He repays the gratitude of that Day.”"
"9448","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the morning: “O God, by you we have become in the morning, by you we have entered the evening, and by you we have We live, and by you we die, and to you is the resurrection.”"
"9449","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, he said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Muslim ibn Ziyad, the client of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, told me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says in the morning: Oh God, I I bear witness to You, and I bear witness to the bearers of Your throne, and to Your angels, and to all of Your creation, that You are God, there is no god but You, You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad Your servant and Messenger, God freed a quarter of that day from the Fire. If he said it four times, God freed him from the Fire of that day.” Amr bin Uthman and Kathir bin Ubaid disagreed with him regarding the wording of the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9450","Amr bin Uthman and Kathir bin Ubaid told me, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Muslim bin Ziyad, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever says in the morning: O God, I call you to witness, and I call to witness the bearers of your throne, and your angels, and all of your creation, Indeed, You are God, there is no god but You, You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger, except that God forgives him whatever sin befalls him, And if he said it in the evening, may God forgive him for what befell him, meaning that night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9451","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, he said: I heard Amr bin Asim He narrates that he heard Abu Hurairah say: Abu Bakr said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Tell me something that I should say if In the morning and in the evening, he said: “Say: O God, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign. I bear witness that There is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and the evil of Satan and his polytheism, in the morning, and in the evening, and when you go to bed. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9452","Ahmad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Salim Al-Farra’ told him, that Abd al-Hamid, the client of Banu Hashim, told him that his mother told him, and she was serving some of the daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a daughter The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told her that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Say when you wake up in the morning: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, and there is no power Except by God. Whatever God wills happens, and whatever God wills does not happen. I know that God has power over all things, and that God encompasses all things in knowledge. For whoever says them in the morning and mentions a word with its meaning, it will be memorized until the evening, and whoever says it in the evening will be memorized until the morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9453","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Abu Balj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you a word from a treasure beneath Paradise? There is no power nor strength except in God. He says: My servant has submitted and surrendered. Muhammad bin Al-Sa'ib disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abu Dharr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9454","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Shall I not guide you to one of the treasures of Paradise?” I said: Yes, he said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9455","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Anas bin Iyadh told us, on the authority of Abu Mawdud, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, On the authority of Uthman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says: In the name of God, by whose name nothing on earth or in heaven is harmed, and He is the Hearer.” The All-Knowing, so he said it in the evening, no sudden calamity would surprise him until the morning, and if he said it in the morning, no sudden calamity would surprise him until the evening. \. Abdullah bin Maslamah disagreed with him. He narrated it"","" on the authority of Abu Mawdud"","" on the authority of a man"","" on the authority of someone who heard Aban bin Uthman. Muhammad bin Ali told me"","" he said: Al-Qa’nabi told us"","" he said: Abu Mawdud told us"","" on the authority of a man"","" he said: Whoever heard Aban bin Othman"","" saying: I heard Othman bin Affan"","" saying: I heard the Messenger of God"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" and something similar. Abu Abdul Rahman told us: It was narrated on the authority of Aban bin Uthman with a word other than this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9456","Qutaibah told us, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b, On the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: O God, you are my Lord, there is no god Except You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I seek refuge in You by Your grace. And I confess to you my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except you. If he said it after he became certain and died on that day, If he says it in the evening, he will be in Paradise, and if he says it in the evening and dies before the morning, he will be in Paradise.” Al-Walid bin Tha’labah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father"
"9457","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Tha’labah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever says: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your grace and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You. Then he dies on that day or night and enters Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9458","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Hujayra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called on Salman Al-Khair, and he said “Indeed, the Prophet of God wants to give you words with which you will ask the Most Gracious, and desire Him through them, and invoke them by them day and night. Say: O God, I am I ask you for health in faith, faith in good character, success followed by success, mercy from you, well-being, forgiveness from you, and satisfaction.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9459","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Jalil bin Atiya, on the authority of Ja’far bin Maymun, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra told me that he said to his father: O father, I hear you praying every morning: “O God, grant me good health in My body, O God, grant me health in my hearing, O Allah, grant me health in my sight, there is no god but You, three times in the morning, meaning: in the morning, and three times in the evening, and saying: O God I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave. You repeat it three times in the morning, and three times every other time, meaning: in the evening? He said: Yes, my son, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicating for them, so I like to follow his Sunnah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ja`far ibn Maimun is not strong in hadith, and Abu Amir al-Aqdi is trustworthy."
"9460","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say when evening came: “We entered the evening and the evening The kingdom belongs to God, and praise be to God. There is no god but God alone, with no partner. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, miserliness, and evil arrogance. And trial in this world, and torment in the Fire. And when morning comes, he says something like that.” Zubayd added to it, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, citing it as a chain of transmission. He said: “He alone, without a partner.” To Him belongs the dominion, to Him is praise, and He has power over all things.”"
"9461","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad informed me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Qasim, the client of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that he said while he was in the land of the Romans: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things ten times.” God recorded for him ten good deeds, erased from him ten bad deeds, granted him the value of ten slaves, and God protected him from Satan and from He said it on the evening he had something similar to that.”"
"9462","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things, a hundred times a day. He had the reward of ten slaves, and one hundred good deeds were recorded for him, and one hundred bad deeds were erased from him, and it was for him a protection against Satan on that day. That is until the evening, and no one brought anything better than what he brought except someone who did more than that.” Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind disagreed with him regarding the wording of the hadith."
"9463","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah Al-Attar Al-Basri told us, he said: Makki bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God Alone, He has no partner. To Him belongs dominion, and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. Ten times in the morning, one hundred good deeds were recorded for him in it. One hundred bad deeds were erased from him with it, and it was the protection of a slave, and his day was preserved with it until the evening, and whoever said it like that when the evening “He had something like that.” Suhail bin Abi Saleh disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abi Saleh, on the authority of Abi Ayyash, Zayd bin Al-Nu’man."
"9464","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Ayyash al-Zarqi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but God, alone does not A partner to Him, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. He had as much as a slave from the descendants of Ishmael, and ten good deeds, and ten bad deeds were removed from him, and he was on guard from Satan until the evening, and when the evening came like that until the morning,” he saw. A man of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw what the sleeper saw, and he said: O Messenger of God, Abu Ayyash narrates such-and-such about you? He said: “Abu Ayyash spoke the truth.”"
"9465","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Asim told me, he said: Wabar told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Maymun told me, On the authority of Yaqoub bin Asim that he heard two men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say “No servant has ever said: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things, sincering his soul with it.” Verifying with it his heart and his tongue, unless the gates of heaven will be opened for him until God looks at who said it, and it is the right of a servant whom God looks upon to \He gives him what he asks for.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9466","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman told me, he said: Zayd bin Ali told us, he said: Ja’far, meaning Ibn Burqan, told us, on the authority of more than one person, Ibn Bishr, And others, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, narrating the hadith to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “ Whoever says: There is no god but God, and God is the greatest, there is no god but God alone, without any partner, there is no god but God, to Him belongs the kingdom and to Him is praise, there is no god Except God, and there is no power nor strength except in God. He crossed them five times with his fingers, then said: Whoever says them in a day, a night, or a month? Then he died on that day, or that night, or in that month, and his sin was forgiven.” Hamza al-Zayat disagreed with him in his chain of transmission and text."
"9467","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Aghar, Abu Muslim. He bore witness against Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed, that they bore witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If the servant says: No There is no god but God alone. He said: My servant spoke the truth, there is no god but Me alone. And when he said: There is no god but God, He has no partner, he said: My servant spoke the truth, no. There is no god but Me, I have no partner, and when he says: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, he says: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god but Me, to Me is the dominion. To me is praise, and when he says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah, he says: He says: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god but Me, there is no might or “There is no strength except in Me.” Abu Ishaq said: Then Al-Aghar said something that I did not understand, so I said to Abu Ja’far: What did he say? He said: “Whoever is provided with them at death will not be touched by fire.”"
"9468","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, he said: I bear witness to Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed, that they bore witness against the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I bear witness against them, that he said: “The servant, when He said: There is no god but God, and God is greatest. His Lord, Blessed and Most High, believed him.” Shu'bah disagreed with him, so the hadith stopped and did not mention Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9469","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: He told us and mentioned Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: “God verifies the servant with five things that he says. When he says: There is no god but God, he says: My servant is truthful. And when he says: There is no god but God alone. He said: My servant spoke the truth, and when he said: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner. He said: My servant spoke the truth, and when he said: There is no god but God and God. Akbar, he said: My servant has spoken the truth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9470","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you hears the muezzin reciting the tashahhud, say Like he said.” Malik bin Anas disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid L5639, on the authority of Abu Sa’id (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9471","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you hear the caller, say what he says.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct hadith is the hadith of Malik, and the hadith of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq is wrong, and this Abd al-Rahman is called: servants. Ibn Ishaq, and there is nothing wrong with him, and Abd al-Rahman Ibn Ishaq, a group of the people of Kufa narrated from him, and he is a weak hadith, by God. I know"
"9472","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of his paternal aunt Umm Habibah, who said: “Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with me and he heard the call to prayer, he would say as he said until he remained silent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9473","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Abu Malih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba bin Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his paternal aunt, Umm Habibah bint Abu Sufyan, who said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with her in On that day, he heard the muezzin giving the call to prayer and he said as he said until he finished.” Shu`bah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Bishr, Ja`far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Umm Habibah, and he did not mention Abdullah ibn Threshold"
"9474","Muhammad ibn Bashhar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Umm Habiba, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When he heard the muezzin, he would say as he said until he remained silent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9475","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabi’ah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard a man giving the call to prayer while on a journey. He said: God is greatest, God is greatest. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God is great, God is great.” He said: I bear witness that there is no god but God. He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” He said: I bear witness that there is no god but God. Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: “I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9476","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Asbagh bin Faraj told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told me, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Hilal, that Yahya bin Abdul Rahman narrated to him, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of his father, he said: While we were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he heard a man in the valley saying: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger. God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And I bear witness. No one bears witness to it unless he is free of polytheism.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9477","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Jahm al-Thaqafi informed us, he said: Ismail bin Ja`far told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman bin Yasaf, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the muezzin says: God is great, God is great, and he says One of you said: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Then he said: Come to prayer. He said: There is no power nor strength except in God. Then he said: Come to prayer. On the farmer, he said: There is no power nor strength except in God, then he said: God is great, God is great, he said: God is great, God is great, then he said: No. There is no god but Allah. He said: There is no god but Allah. Paradise is guaranteed for him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9478","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: A partner told us, and Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: A partner told us. On the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the call to prayer, he said Like what he says, he said: When he reached the funeral, he greeted the prayer, he greeted the farmer, he said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” The pronunciation is for Ali, and it was not mentioned: Hayy Ali al-Falah. Sufyan Al-Thawri disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Harith, his father. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the muezzin, he would say something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9479","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Dhar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no power nor strength except in God, one of the treasures of Paradise.”"
"9480","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Hayy bin Abdullah, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli told him, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that a man said: O Messenger of God, do the muezzins prefer us? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say as they say, and when you have finished, ask and it will be given to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9481","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Ka’b bin Alqamah informed me, that he heard Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, client of Nafi’ bin Amr al-Qurashi, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When you hear the muezzin, say what he says, and pray for me, for he is the one who prayed for me, may God bless him and grant him peace ten times.” Then ask me the means, for it is a status in Paradise that is only appropriate for one of the servants of God, and I hope that I am him, so who He asked me for a means of intercession for him.”"
"9482","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the call: O God, Lord of this perfect call and prayer The List, give Muhammad the means and the virtue, and raise him to the praised station which You promised him, intercession will be permitted for him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9483","Hajib bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, he said: Dawud bin Qays told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abdullah Al-Mujmar, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, how can we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Abraham and the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy.” Glorious and peaceful, as you have learned.” Malik bin Anas disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Nu`aym bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9484","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a reading of it and its pronunciation, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Naim bin Abdullah Al-Mujmar, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Ansari informed him, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, he said: He came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the gathering of Saad bin Ubadah, and Bashir bin Saad said to him: God has commanded us to pray for you, O Messenger of God. So how do we pray for you, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent until we wished he had not asked him, then he said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Abraham, and you have blessed Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as You have blessed Abraham’s family in the worlds. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Muhammad bin Ibrahim disagreed with him regarding the wording of the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9485","Ahmad ibn Bakkar informed me, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd God, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you. We have known him, so how can we pray for you? May God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless you? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent for an hour, then he said: “You say: O God, bless Muhammad the unlettered Prophet, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham. And bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, as You blessed Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9486","Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Bishr, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al Ansari, who said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: God has commanded us to send blessings upon you. We greet you, but as for peace, we know it, so how can we pray upon you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham’s family. O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham’s family.” Abdullah bin Aoun disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Bishr, with a mursal message. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9487","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Bishr said: They said: O Messenger of God, we have learned how to greet you, so how about praying? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham’s family. O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham’s family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9488","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muja’ bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Mawhib, On the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, how is the prayer upon you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Khaled bin Salamah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Zayd bin Kharijah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9489","Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed told me in his hadith, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Khaled bin Salamah, on the authority of Musa bin Talha He said: I asked Zayd bin Kharijah. He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Pray for me and strive to supplicate, and say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9490","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, he said: He said: Ka'b bin Ujrah, can I not give you a gift? We said: O Messenger of God, we know how to greet you, so how do we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Abraham. O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Muhammad. Abraham, you are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9491","Ahmad bin Al-Khalil told us, he said: Khaled, who is Ibn Mukhlid Al-Qatwani, told us, he said: Suleiman, meaning Ibn Bilal, told us, he said: Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Ali bin Hussein speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “The miserly person is the one before whom I am mentioned and he does not pray for me.”"
"9492","Suleiman bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Suleiman told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of his father: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The miserly person is the one before whom I was mentioned and does not pray.” “Ali.” Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib Sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9493","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, said: Ali bin Abi Talib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The miserly person who, if I am mentioned He did not pray for me.”"
"9494","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf told us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A people has never sat together and dispersed without sending blessings upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And peace be upon them, unless they disperse, stinking of the odor of carrion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9495","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr Ibn Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr Ibn Sulaym al-Zarqi, he said: Abu Humayd al-Sa’idi told me that they said: O Messenger of God, how? May we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and his wives and his offspring, as You bless the family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad and his wives and his offspring.” Just as You blessed the family of Abraham, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9496","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Suleiman The servant of Al-Hasan bin Ali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day And the glad tidings appeared on his face, and he said: “Gabriel came to me and said: Is it not your satisfaction, O Muhammad, that no one from your nation prays over you except that I prayed?” ten times upon him, and no one from your nation will greet you except that you greet him ten times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9497","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Abu Salamah, who is Al-Mughirah bin Muslim Al-Khurasani, told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq. On the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever I am mentioned to, let him pray for me, and whoever prays for me once, may God’s prayers be upon him.” “Tenth” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9498","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: Buraid bin Abu Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays one prayer over me, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He performed ten prayers upon him, and He removed from him ten bad deeds thereby, and raised him ten degrees because of them.” Mukhlid bin Yazid disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam Al-Basri, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Owner"
"9499","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam al-Basri, he said: I was accompanying Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan in a camp, and he said: Anas bin Malik told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays One prayer upon me, may God bless him ten times, and remove ten sins from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9500","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, who is the son of Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Umair Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father He was Badri. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever of my nation prays upon me sincerely from his heart, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him ten times.” Prayers, and raised him ten degrees by them, and recorded for him ten good deeds thereby, and erased from him ten bad deeds.” Abu Osama Hammad bin Osama disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Saeed bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Umair, on the authority of his uncle. Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Umair. Bin Uqba bin Niyar, on the authority of his uncle Abu Burdah bin Niyar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So he mentioned something similar to it."
"9501","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has traveling angels who convey to me peace from my nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9502","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurayi, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A supplication is not rejected between the call to prayer and the iqama.”"
"9503","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki` and Abu Nu`aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A supplication is not rejected between the call to prayer and the iqama.”"
"9504","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The supplication between the call to prayer and the iqamah is not rejected.” Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi stopped him, Ishaq ibn Mansour informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Anas. . . . . . . . His saying. Sulayman al-Taymi stopped him, but there was disagreement over his wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9505","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The supplication between the call to prayer And the residence is not rejected.”"
"9506","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When the iqamah for prayer is The gates of heaven were opened, and prayers were answered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9507","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Abdullah bin Qais, he told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the muezzin: And I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, without any partner.” His, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am satisfied with God as Lord, and with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, as Messenger, and with Islam as religion. He will be forgiven. \His sin\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9508","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And when he entered the toilet, he would say: “I seek refuge in God from evil and evil things.”"
"9509","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and Ibn Mahdi told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, On the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These gardens are dying, so if one of you enters the toilet, let him say: I seek refuge in God from wickedness and evil things.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9510","Mu'mal bin Hisham told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Ibn Abi Orouba told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, On the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These courtyards are dying, so if one of you wants to enter the toilet... Let him say: I seek refuge in God from evil and evil things.” Yazid bin Zuray’ differed from him. He narrated it, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Qasim Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam."
"9511","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Qasim Al-Shaybani. On the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These crowds are dying, so if one of you enters the toilet, let him say: “I seek refuge in God from evil and evil.”"
"9512","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, on the authority of Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qasim Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These courtyards are dying, so if any of you enters or wants to enter, Let him say: I seek refuge in God from evil and evil things.”"
"9513","Ahmad bin Nasr told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave the feces except that he said: “Your forgiveness.”"
"9514","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Al-Mu`tamir, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, informed us, saying: I heard Abbad, meaning Ibn Abbad ibn Alqamah, He says: I heard Abu Majliz say: Abu Musa said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he performed ablution, so I heard him supplicate, saying: Oh God, forgive me my sins, expand my home for me, and bless my livelihood.” He said: I said: O Prophet of God, I heard you praying such-and-such. He said: “Did he leave anything behind?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9515","Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakan told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: He told us Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever performs ablution, He said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. It was written on parchment and then printed with a stamp, so it was not It will be broken until the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the correct view is definite. Muhammad bin Jaafar disagreed with him and stopped him. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, he said: I heard Abu Majliz narrating, On the authority of Qais bin Abbad, on the authority of Abu Saeed. . . . . . . . . His saying. Abu Abdul Rahman said: It was also narrated by Sufyan bin Saeed bin Masruq Al-Thawri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9516","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: “Whoever performs ablution and completes his ablution, then says: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you. God placed a seal on it, then it was raised under the Throne and it was not broken until the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9517","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Zahra bin Ma’bed told me, His cousin, his father’s brother Laha, told him that Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani told him, saying: Omar bin Al-Khattab told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then raises his gaze to the sky and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and He alone does not A partner for him, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. The eight gates of Paradise were opened for him and he may enter through whichever one he wishes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9518","Ali bin Sahl told me, he said: Mu’mal told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he left his house, he would say: “O God, I seek refuge in You lest I slip or go astray, or be unjust or wronged, or I am ignorant or I am being ignored.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake: Asim on the authority of al-Shu’abi, and the correct thing is: Shu’bah on the authority of Mansour, and Ma’mal ibn Ismail Kathir. The error. Bahz ibn Asad disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Shu`bi. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9519","Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his house, he would say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from slipping or going astray, or “Whether he is unjust or I am wronged, or he is ignorant or he is ignorant of me.” It was narrated by Sufyan and he added to it: “In the name of God, I put my trust in God.”"
"9520","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he left his house, he would say: “In the name of God, I put my trust in God. Oh God, we seek refuge in You from straying or going astray. Or we are wronged or we are wronged, or we are ignorant or we are treated ignorantly.” It was narrated by Zubaid, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . . . . . . Likewise, he did not mention “In the Name of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9521","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man leaves his house and says: In the name of God, I trust in God, there is no power or There is no strength except in God. Then it will be said to him: ‘It is sufficient for you. You have been guided, protected, and sufficient.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9522","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Al-Dahhak told us, he said: Saeed Al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you enters the mosque, he should greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, open I have the doors of your mercy, and when he comes out, let him greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, keep me away from Satan.” Muhammad bin Ajlan disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ka`b, his saying (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9523","Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “The Ka’b Al-Ahbar, he said: “O Abu Hurairah, keep two commandments from me that I advise you to do: When you enter the mosque, pray for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And say: O God, open for me the doors of your mercy, and when you leave the mosque, pray for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, protect me. From Satan.” Ibn Abi Dhib disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ka’b (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9524","Issa bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun has neither risen nor set on a better day than Friday,” then he presented On us is the heel. Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned an hour on Friday that does not coincide with a believer who prays and asks God. He did not give him anything. Ka’b said: He who honored him spoke the truth, and I am telling you two, so do not forget them. When you enter the mosque, greet the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and say: Oh God, open for me the doors of your mercy, and when you go out, greet the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and say: Oh God. Protect me from Satan.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Abi Dhib is more reliable to us than Muhammad bin Ajlan and al-Dahhak bin Uthman in Sa`id al-Maqbari. And his hadith is more deserving of what is correct in our view, and God grant us success. Ibn Ajlan’s hadiths were mixed with Sa’id al-Maqbari, what Sa’id narrated. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Sa`id, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and other of Sa`id’s sheikhs, so Ibn Ajlan made it All of them are on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Ibn Ajlan are trustworthy, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9525","Muhammad bin Nasr told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim Ibn Aidh, on the authority of Aamir Ibn Saad, on the authority of Saad, that a man came to pray while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying for us, and he said when he finished To the class: Oh God, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, he said: “Who is the speaker above?” “The man said: It is me, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the path of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9526","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of a man called Abd al-Rahman bin al-Rammah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awsaja, one from the other, on the authority of Aisha, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he would say: “O God, you are the peace.” And from you is peace, blessed be you, O possessor of majesty and honor.” Yazid bin Harun disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Walid, on the authority of Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9527","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Walid, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was not The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would sit after prayer, except insofar as he would say: “O God, you are the peace and from you is peace. Blessed are you, O Lord of Majesty.” And honor.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Al-Walid, his name is: Abdullah bin Al-Harith, Khalid bin Mihran Al-Hadha’ and Asim bin Suleiman narrated from him."
"9528","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would greet him, he would say: “O God, you are peace and from you is peace. Blessed is the One of majesty and honor.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9529","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman told me, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim and Khalid, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the salaam from his prayer, “O God, you are the peace.” And from you is peace, blessed be the Possessor of majesty and honor.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Shu’bah and Yazid bin Harun is more deserving in our view. The first hadith is correct, and the first hadith is wrong, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9530","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Awsaja bin Al-Rammah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not sit when he said the salaam, except as much as he would say: “O God, you are the peace.” And the place of peace, blessed be You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” Shu'bah bin Al-Hajjaj gave it as an endowment"
"9531","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Awsaja bin Ar-Rammah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, that when he finished his prayer, he would say: “O God, peace from you and peace to you, Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9532","Al-Hussein bin Bishr told us, in Tarsus, we wrote about him, he said: Muhammad bin Himyar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi at the end of every obligatory prayer, it will not prevent him from entering Paradise unless he dies.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9533","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, he said: Dawud al-Taffawi told me, on the authority of Abu Muslim al-Bajali. On the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicating at the end of prayer, saying: “O God, our Lord and Lord of all things, I I bear witness that You are the Lord, You alone have no partner, O God, our Lord and the Lord of all things. I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, O God, our Lord and the Lord of all things. Everything. I bear witness that all servants are brothers. Oh God, our Lord and Lord of everything, make me and my family loyal to You at every hour in this world. And the Hereafter, Possessor of majesty and honor. Listen and respond. God is the Greatest, the Greatest. God is the light of the heavens and the earth. God is the Greatest, the Greatest. My suffice is God is the best disposer of affairs, God is the greatest, God is the greatest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9534","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of a servant of Umm Salamah, On the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say after dawn when he prayed: “O God, I ask you for useful knowledge and good deeds.” accepted, and a good provision.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9535","Ahmad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Zazan, he said: A man from the Ansar told me, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying at the end of the prayer: “O God, forgive me and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Most Relenting, the Forgiving,” until he reached A hundred times"
"9536","Muhammad bin Hisham Al-Sadusi told me, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Husayn, he said: I heard Hilal bin Yasaf narrates, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Prayer, Khaled said: Then something broke down for me, then he said: “My Lord, forgive me, and turn to me, for You are the Most Relenting, the Most Merciful” a hundred times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9537","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Rabi’ Khurasani told me about Al-Masissa, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of a man from the Ansar whose name he forgot, that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying two rak’ahs Duha, when he sat down, I heard him say: “My Lord, forgive me and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Forgiver, the Merciful,” until he reached a hundred times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9538","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Muslim, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of a man from the Ansar who said: I passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him while he was praying the forenoon prayer, and I heard him saying: “O God, forgive me, and have mercy on me, for You are the Forgiver, the Forgiver,” until I counted it a hundred times. Khalid bin Abdullah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Aisha."
"9539","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, he said: Khaled bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the forenoon prayer, then he said: “O God, forgive me and accept my repentance, for You are The Most Merciful, the Forgiving” until he said it a hundred times. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Shu`bah, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim, and Abbad bin al-Awwam is more worthy of authenticity in our view than the hadith of Khaled. By God, grant us success. Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman was mixed up at the end of his life. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9540","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, which supplication should I hear? He said: “The middle of the night, and after the prescribed prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9541","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Haywa bin Shurayh told us, he said: I heard Uqba bin Muslim Al-Tajibi, he says: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli told me, on the authority of al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He took him by the hand one day, then said: “O Muadh, by God, I love you.” Then Muadh said to him: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, and I And God I love you. He said: “I advise you, O Muadh, not to stop saying at the end of every prayer: O God, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well.” \. Muadh al-Sanabihi recommended this"","" Al-Sanabihi recommended it to Abu Abd al-Rahman"","" and Abu Abd al-Rahman Uqba bin Muslim (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9542","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks God for Paradise three times, Paradise will say: O God, admit him to Paradise, and whoever seeks protection from God From the Fire three times, and the Fire said: Oh God, protect him from the Fire.”"
"9543","Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Hassan Al-Kanani, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Harith bin Muslim Al-Tamimi He told them, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “When you pray the morning prayer, say before you speak: O God, reward me.” from the Fire seven times, for if you die on that day, God will record for you a protection from the Fire, so when you pray the Maghrib prayer, say before She says: “O God, save me from the Fire seven times, for if you die that night, God will record for you protection from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9544","Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ibn Abu Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever says at the end of the morning prayer: There is no god but God, alone... A partner to Him, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. Be to Him equal to four slaves from the descendants of Ishmael.” Endowed by Ismail bin Abi Khaled (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9545","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, he said: “Whoever said: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. He has the equivalent of four slaves.” I said to him: Who told you? He said: Amr bin Maymun, so I met Amr bin Maymun, and I said: Who told you? He said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, so I met Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, and I said: Who told you? He said: Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Hilal bin Yasaf disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, L1405, on the authority of Ibn Masoud."
"9546","Hajib bin Sulayman told me, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud. He said: “Whoever says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things, has The equivalent of four slaves from the descendants of Ishmael.” It was narrated by Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khathim, and he said about it: “Ten times"
"9547","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Maysara told me, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. And He has power over all things, ten times equal to four slaves. It was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khathim, and Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Abd God"
"9548","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun. And Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “Because I say: There is no god but Allah. He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is Able to do all things ten times is dearer to me than freeing four slaves.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: There was disagreement over Mansour ibn al-Mu’tamir regarding this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9549","Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Mansour told me, Abu Al-Muhyah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, Alone with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise. In His hand is goodness, and He has power over all things. He had four freed men from the descendants of Ishmael.” Zaida bin Qudamah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub"
"9550","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Amr Ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He recited Say, He is God, One, as if he had recited a third of the Qur’an. And whoever says: There is no god but God, Alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. And He has power over all things, ten times, be to Him as equal to a breath.” It was narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, L6271, without this wording."
"9551","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God alone, without any partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. Every day, a hundred Once upon a time, the Day of Resurrection came over every worker except the one who did more.” Abu Ishaq Al-Subai’i disagreed with them. He narrated it, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, his statement (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9552","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, On the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things, ten times greater in reward or better than one who freed four souls from his children. “Ishmael.” Zayd bin Abi Anisa disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, his saying. Muhammad bin Jabla told me, he said: Abdullah bin Jafar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he is Ibn Amr, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Unaysa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, who said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah... . Abu Balaj disagreed with them. He narrated it, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, and with a different wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9553","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Al-Nu’man Al-Hakam bin Abdullah told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maimun speaking, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone with no partner, to Him belongs the kingdom and to Him belongs Praise, and He has power over all things. His sins have been forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea.” Muhammad bin Jaafar disagreed with him regarding the wording of the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9554","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah He said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, and God is great, and praise be to God, and glory be to God greatly, and there is no power nor strength except in God, His sins have been forgiven, even if they were more than the foam of the sea.” Abu Yunus Hatim bin Abi raised it as a small narration. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, Abi Yunus al-Qushayri, on the authority of Abu Balj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . . . . . . Like him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9555","Ja`far bin Imran informed us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Mansour, he said: Al-Hussein bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, Alone, He has no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is Able to do all things. Ten times, they are equal to a breath."
"9556","Ja`far bin Imran told us, he said: Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Asim bin Mansour Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein Al-Makki, On the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Muadh, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever said when He ends the morning prayer: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things ten times. Before he spoke, ten good deeds were recorded for him for them, ten bad deeds were erased from him, and he was raised ten degrees because of them, and they were just for him. Ten breaths, and they were a guard for him from Satan, and a protection from harm, and no sin befell him on that day except associating others with God, and whoever He said to them when he finished the afternoon prayer, “He was given something like that on his night.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Husayn ibn Asim is unknown, and Shahr ibn Hawshab is weak. Ibn Aoun was asked about the hadith of Shahr, and he said: They left him for a month, and Shu'bah had a bad opinion of him, and Yahya al-Qattan left him. Zaid bin Abi Unaisa disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Abu Dharr."
"9557","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Hakim bin Saif told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever says at the end of the Fajr prayer while he is on his second leg, before speaking: There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and Praise, He gives life and causes death, in His hand is goodness, and He has power over all things ten times. God recorded for him a good deed for every one of them he said. A bad deed was erased from him, and he was raised in rank because of it, and for every single thing he said he freed a slave, and on that day he was in the protection of all. Hated, and protected from Satan, and no sin would overtake him on that day except associating others with God.”"
"9558","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: Abd Ibn Al-Zubayr praised God at the end of the prayer, saying: “There is no god but God, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things.” There is no god but God, and we worship none but Him. To Him is grace and to Him is favour, and to Him is good praise. There is no god but God, sincere in religion to Him even if he hates it. “The disbelievers.” Then Ibn al-Zubayr says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to rejoice in them at the end of prayer."
"9559","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman informed us, he said: Hushaym informed us, he said: Al-Mughirah informed us. Another reported, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Wardad, the writer of Al-Mughirah: that Muawiyah wrote to Al-Mughirah, “Write to me with a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Al-Mughirah wrote to him, saying, “I heard him saying when he finished praying: ‘There is no god but God, alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things” three times. Abu Awanah Al-Waddah disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, and he did not mention a narration."
"9560","Muhammad bin Muammar told me, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that Muawiyah wrote to him: Write to me about what you heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say at the end of prayer. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying at the end of prayer: “There is no god but God. He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. And He is Able to do all things. O God, there is no deterrent to what You have given and no giver of what You have withheld, and no one who is serious can benefit from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9561","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, he said: I heard Musaab bin Saad said: Saad used to teach us these words and narrate them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, I seek refuge in You from Stinginess, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being sent back to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9562","Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun Al-Awdi said: Saad used to teach his sons these words as a teacher teaches boys, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to seek refuge in them after the prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from turning away To the most miserable age, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.” So I narrated it to Musaab and he believed him. Abu Ishaq disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9563","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ghazwan informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr Ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things: from stinginess, cowardice, and bad life. And the temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” Israel disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9564","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to seek refuge from the five things: cowardice, miserliness, and bad life. And the temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” Narrated by Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9565","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from miserliness, cowardice, and temptation.” And the torment of the grave.” Sent by Sufyan bin Saeed. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeks refuge. . . . . . . . sender (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9566","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Hafs bin Maysarah told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b swore by God who parted the sea to Moses: “Indeed, we find that David is a prophet By God, when he finished his prayer, he would say: O God, make right for me my religion which You have made for me a protection, and make right for me my world in which You have made my livelihood. Oh God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your wrath, and I seek refuge, then he mentioned a word that means, in Your pardon from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in You from You, there is no objection. “For what You have given, and there is no giver for what You have withheld, and no one will be of any benefit to you.” He said: Ka'b told me that Suhayb told him that Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say them when he finished his prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9567","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Qudama told us, on the authority of Jasra, she said: Aisha told me, she said: A Jewish woman came to me and said: The torment of the grave is due to urine. She said: You lied, so she said: Yes, and we will repay from it. The skin and the clothes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to pray and our voices rose. He said: “What is this, Aisha?” So she told him what she said, and he said: “She has spoken the truth.” He did not pray after that day except that he said at the end of the prayer: “Lord of Gabriel, and Lord of Michael and Israfil. Save me from the heat of the Fire and the torment of the grave.”"
"9568","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abu Amr, he said: Shaddad Abu Ammar told me, that Abu Asma Al-Rahbi He told him that he heard Thawban talking that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his prayer, he asked forgiveness three times and said: “O God You are peace and from you is peace. Blessed are you, O Possessor of majesty and honor.”"
"9569","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of my father Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abu Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the tasbih will complete the morning prayer one hundred times.” “Tasbihah, and say one hundred times of Allah, his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea.”"
"9570","Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, on the authority of Makki ibn Ibrahim, he said: Yaqub ibn Ata’ informed us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Alqamah ibn Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says one hundred tasbihs at the end of the morning prayer And he recited a hundred halilas, and his sins were forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Yaqoub bin Ata bin Abi Rabah is weak, Abdul Wahhab bin Mujahid is abandoned in hadith, and Abdullah bin Tawoos is trustworthy and trustworthy, Abdullah bin Saeed bin Jubayr is trustworthy and trustworthy, and Ikrimah, the client of Ibn Abbas, trustworthy and one of the most knowledgeable people, he said. Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid"
